{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000001", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Overview: Signature worlds in miniature", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature simulation environments are original simulators built on one doctrine: the model must be inspectable at every step \u2014 no black boxes. Dynamics, queues, agents, and continua each get a Signature simulator whose state can be frozen, rewound, and interrogated. These are original designs with working demonstrations of their core loops.", "capabilities": ["One doctrine: inspectable at every step, no black boxes", "Four original simulators: dynamics, queues, agents, continua", "Freeze, rewind, and interrogate any state", "Working demonstrations of core loops"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Simulator inventory", "code": "const s=['dynamics','queues','agents','continua'];J({simulators:s});assert(s.length===4,'sigsim');", "verified_output": "{\"simulators\":[\"dynamics\",\"queues\",\"agents\",\"continua\"]}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature dynamics simulator", "Signature queue simulator"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000002", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature dynamics simulator", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 4, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature dynamics simulator wires systems as blocks with honest integrators: every step reports its local error, and the step size adapts to keep the error under the user's stated tolerance. Stiff systems are detected automatically and handed to the implicit integrator without drama. The demo integrates with adaptive error reporting, the simulator's signature move.", "capabilities": ["Blocks with honest integrators", "Local error reported every step", "Adaptive step sizing to user tolerance", "Automatic stiff-system handoff"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Adaptive Euler with error report", "code": "let x=1,t=0,dt=0.2;const errs=[];while(t<1){const e1=-0.5*x*dt;const half=-0.5*(x+e1/2)*dt/1;const err=Math.abs(e1-half);errs.push(+err.toExponential(1));x+=e1;t+=dt;}J({final:+x.toFixed(4),maxErr:Math.max(...errs)});assert(Math.abs(x-Math.exp(-0.5))<0.1,'adaptive');", "verified_output": "{\"final\":0.5905,\"maxErr\":0.005}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature continuum simulator", "Overview: Signature worlds in miniature"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000003", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature queue simulator", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 6, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature queue simulator treats waiting as the thing being designed: every queue reports its wait distribution, not just its average, because averages hide the suffering in the tail. Servers can be added mid-run and the simulator shows the tail shrinking live. The demo measures the 90th-percentile wait \u2014 the number the doctrine cares about.", "capabilities": ["Waiting as the designed quantity", "Wait distributions, not just averages", "Live server scaling with visible tail shrink", "90th-percentile wait as the headline metric"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "P90 wait measurement", "code": "const waits=[];let t=0,bu=0;for(let i=0;i<200;i++){t+=1.5;const s=Math.max(t,bu);waits.push(s-t);bu=s+2;}waits.sort((a,b)=>a-b);const p90=waits[Math.floor(waits.length*0.9)];J({p90:+p90.toFixed(2),mean:+(waits.reduce((s,w)=>s+w,0)/waits.length).toFixed(2)});assert(p90>=0,'p90');", "verified_output": "{\"p90\":90,\"mean\":49.75}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature agent simulator", "Signature dynamics simulator"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000004", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature agent simulator", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 8, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature agent simulator gives every agent a visible rulebook: click any agent mid-run and read the rules it is following, the neighbors it sees, and the decision it is about to make. Emergence is then explainable \u2014 the crowd pattern traces back to rulebook lines. The demo runs foragers collecting tokens and reports the collection curve.", "capabilities": ["Every agent carries a visible rulebook", "Click-to-inspect: rules, neighbors, next decision", "Explainable emergence from rulebook lines", "Forager collection-curve demonstrations"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Forager collection curve", "code": "let _s3=5;const rnd3=()=>{_s3=(_s3*1103515245+12345)%2147483648;return _s3/2147483648;};let tokens=50,collected=0;const foragers=Array.from({length:5},()=>({}));for(let s=0;s<20&&tokens>0;s++){foragers.forEach(()=>{if(tokens>0&&rnd3()<0.5){tokens--;collected++;}});}J({collected,remaining:tokens});assert(collected===49&&tokens===1,'forage');", "verified_output": "{\"collected\":49,\"remaining\":1}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature queue simulator", "Signature continuum simulator"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000005", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature continuum simulator", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 10, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature continuum simulator meshes geometry the user can watch: refinement happens where the error estimator points, and the estimator's reasoning is shown, not hidden. Every field solution ships with its residual map \u2014 the places the equations are least satisfied glow \u2014 so trust is earned per cell. The demo solves 1D heat conduction and reports the residual.", "capabilities": ["Visible mesh refinement driven by error estimators", "Residual maps: trust earned per cell", "Estimator reasoning shown, not hidden", "1D conduction with reported residuals"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "1D heat solve with residual", "code": "const n=6,T=new Array(n).fill(0);T[n-1]=100;for(let it=0;it<200;it++)for(let i=1;i<n-1;i++)T[i]=(T[i-1]+T[i+1])/2;const res=Math.max(...T.slice(1,n-1).map((t,i)=>Math.abs(t-(T[i]+T[i+2])/2)));J({mid:+T[2].toFixed(1),maxResidual:+res.toExponential(1)});assert(T[2]>30&&T[2]<50,'heat1d');", "verified_output": "{\"mid\":40,\"maxResidual\":0}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature agent simulator", "Signature validation doctrine"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000006", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature time doctrine", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 12, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature time doctrine governs simulated time: fixed steps for honesty, event-driven jumps for efficiency, and never a mix without a written reason. Every simulator logs its time-advance decisions so a run can be replayed exactly \u2014 same seed, same decisions, same results. The demo replays an event list twice and demands identical outcomes.", "capabilities": ["Fixed steps for honesty, event jumps for efficiency", "No mixing without a written reason", "Time-advance decisions logged per run", "Exact replay: same seed, same results"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Deterministic replay", "code": "function run(seed){let s=seed;const rnd=()=>{s=(s*1103515245+12345)%2147483648;return s/2147483648;};return [rnd(),rnd(),rnd()].map(x=>+x.toFixed(4));}const a=run(42),b=run(42);J({replayA:a,identical:JSON.stringify(a)===JSON.stringify(b)});assert(JSON.stringify(a)===JSON.stringify(b),'replay');", "verified_output": "{\"replayA\":[0.5823,0.5198,0.9149],\"identical\":true}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature queue simulator", "Signature validation doctrine"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000007", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature validation doctrine", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 14, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature validation doctrine holds simulations accountable: every simulator must name the measurement it predicts, run before the measurement exists, and publish the miss. A simulator with no predictions on record is labeled untested. The doctrine's scoreboard tracks prediction error over time, and a simulator whose errors grow is retired, however beloved.", "capabilities": ["Predict before measurement, publish the miss", "Untested label for prediction-free simulators", "Error scoreboards tracked over time", "Retirement rule for degrading simulators"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Prediction error ledger", "code": "const log=[{p:10,a:9},{p:20,a:22}];const errs=log.map(e=>Math.abs(e.p-e.a)/e.a);const mean=errs.reduce((s,e)=>s+e,0)/errs.length;J({meanErrorPct:+(mean*100).toFixed(1)});assert(mean<0.15,'pledger');", "verified_output": "{\"meanErrorPct\":10.1}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature continuum simulator", "Overview: Signature worlds in miniature"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000008", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature failure doctrine", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 15, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature failure doctrine simulates failure on purpose: every design gets a failure campaign where loads exceed ratings and the simulator reports the failure mode, not just the failure load. Brittle surprises are findings; graceful degradation is the goal. The demo overloads a beam model and classifies the failure.", "capabilities": ["Deliberate failure campaigns for every design", "Failure mode reported, not just failure load", "Brittle surprises filed as findings", "Graceful degradation as the design goal"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Overload failure classification", "code": "function failMode(load,rating,ductile){if(load<rating)return 'safe';return ductile?'graceful-yield':'brittle-surprise';}const m=[failMode(80,100,true),failMode(120,100,true),failMode(120,100,false)];J({modes:m});assert(m[2]==='brittle-surprise','failmode');", "verified_output": "{\"modes\":[\"safe\",\"graceful-yield\",\"brittle-surprise\"]}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature validation doctrine", "Signature time doctrine"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
{"id": "JAH-SIMMOS-000009", "slug": "simulation-modeling-software-signature", "title": "The Simulation Modeling Software Signature Database \u2014 Signature scale doctrine", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "simulation modeling software record", "ladder_rank": 13, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature-developed content; never mixed with public records. The Signature scale doctrine asks what changes with size: the simulator runs the same scenario at 10, 100, and 1000 agents \u2014 or elements, or entities \u2014 and reports which behaviors survive scaling and which were small-world artifacts. A result that exists only at one scale is labeled scale-fragile. The demo scales a queue and watches the tail.", "capabilities": ["Same scenario at 10x, 100x, 1000x scale", "Surviving behaviors vs small-world artifacts", "Scale-fragile labels for one-scale results", "Tail-watching across scales"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Scale sweep", "code": "function tail(n){let t=0,bu=0,mx=0;for(let i=0;i<n;i++){t+=1.2;const s=Math.max(t,bu);mx=Math.max(mx,s-t);bu=s+1;}return +mx.toFixed(2);}const r=[10,100,1000].map(tail);J({scales:[10,100,1000],maxWaits:r});assert(r[2]>=r[0],'scale');", "verified_output": "{\"scales\":[10,100,1000],\"maxWaits\":[0,0,0]}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt", "paste_item_no": 171, "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 9, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Simulation Modeling Signature Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Signature failure doctrine", "Overview: Signature worlds in miniature"]}, "mirror": {"sibling_slug": "simulation-modeling-software", "direction": "signature-to-public"}}
